+# Glossary
+
+- **Title**: a catalogue entry (ISBN, material, replacement cost).
+- **Copy**: one physical item of a title, identified by its barcode.
+- **Circulating copy**: a copy that is not withdrawn.
+- **Loan**: a copy lent to a member, from `borrowed_on` to `due_on`.
+- **Replacement cost**: what the library pays to replace a copy of a title; also the cap on all fines on one loan together (renewal fines plus the return fine).
+- **Closed day**: a day the library is shut (Sunday). Never a due date, never a late day.
+- **Late day**: a day after the due date, up to and including the return (or reckoning) day, on which the library is open.
+- **Overdue fine** (fine): charged to an adult member when a copy comes back late: late days × the material's rate, capped at the replacement cost. Children are never fined.
+- **Manual charge** (charge): an amount staff add to a member's account with a reason, e.g. for damage.
+- **Payment**: money a member pays off their balance; never more than they owe.
+- **Account entry**: one fine, charge, payment or no-show fee recorded against a member.
+- **Balance**: what a member owes right now: fines, charges and no-show fees minus payments. Never negative.
+- **Whole cents**: an amount with at most two decimal places.
+- **Account blocked**: the member's balance is at or above the bar for an action, so that action is refused (`AccountBlocked`).
+- **Borrowing bar**: 10.00. At or above it, a member cannot check out.
+- **Hold bar**: 5.00. At or above it, a member cannot place a hold.
+- **Hold**: a member's place in the queue for a title (not a specific copy), asking to have a copy set aside for them.
+- **Hold queue** (queue, line): a title's active holds in the order they were placed; "first in line" is the oldest.
+- **Active hold**: a hold that is waiting or ready.
+- **Waiting hold**: an active hold with no copy yet.
+- **Ready hold**: a hold with a copy set aside on the hold shelf, waiting to be collected.
+- **Hold shelf**: where set-aside copies wait (`CopyStatus.ON_HOLD_SHELF`); only the hold's member can borrow them.
+- **Set aside**: putting a free copy on the hold shelf for the first waiting hold.
+- **Pickup time**: 7 calendar days from the day a copy is set aside, moved past a closed day. The last day to collect is `pickup_by`.
+- **No-show fee**: 1.00, charged when a ready hold expires because the member didn't collect it by `pickup_by`. Children never pay it.
+- **Renewal**: giving an open book loan a fresh full loan period counted from the renewal day, on the same loan (`Loan.renewals` counts them). Renewing an overdue loan charges the fine accrued so far. Not allowed while anyone is waiting for the title, or if the member owes anything. DVDs cannot be renewed.
+- **Renewal limit**: 2. A loan can be renewed at most twice.
+- **Renewal window**: from 5 calendar days before the due date onwards (overdue included); a loan can only be renewed inside it.
+- **Paid up**: a balance of exactly 0.00.
