+# 0001: Member account is a ledger of entries
+
+## Context
+
+Members now owe money: overdue fines, manual staff charges, and later no-show fees
+(ADR 0004) and renewal fines (ADR 0005). Payments reduce what they owe. Staff will
+eventually want to see the history, and waivers may come later.
+
+## Decision
+
+- Each member has one **balance**. It is derived from an append-only list of
+  **account entries** (`AccountEntry`), never stored as a running number.
+- An entry has an id, member, kind (`fine`, `charge`, `payment`; later `no_show`),
+  a positive amount in whole cents, the day it was made, a reason, and the loan it
+  relates to (if any).
+- Balance = sum of non-payment entries − sum of payments. A payment may not exceed
+  the balance, so the balance is never negative and there is no account credit.
+- Amounts are `Decimal` in whole cents and strictly positive. Anything else raises
+  `InvalidAmount`. A manual charge needs a non-blank reason (`InvalidReason`).
+- Every new kind of money owed (no-show fee, renewal fine) is a new entry kind on
+  this same balance, not a separate account.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- History, waivers (a new entry kind) and reports can be added without migrating data.
+- Fines are linked to their loan, so a per-loan rule spanning several charges
+  (see the open question in ADR 0005) can be enforced later.
+- Balance is O(entries) to compute; fine for an in-memory desk system.
