+# 0003: Blocking members who owe too much
+
+## Context
+
+Members who owe money should be stopped from taking more from the library. The
+owner set different thresholds per action.
+
+## Decision
+
+- **Borrowing bar**: `checkout` raises `AccountBlocked` when the balance is
+  10.00 or more (exactly 10.00 is blocked).
+- **Hold bar** (for later, when holds exist): placing a hold raises `AccountBlocked`
+  when the balance is 5.00 or more. It is lower than the borrowing bar on purpose:
+  a hold ties up a copy for someone who already owes the library.
+- Thresholds are per action and live in `lending.policy` (`BORROW_BLOCK_AT`, and
+  later `HOLD_BLOCK_AT`). All blocks use the same error, `AccountBlocked`, and
+  compare with "balance ≥ bar".
+- Only acquiring actions (checkout; later holds) are blocked. Returns, payments and
+  charges always work, so a blocked member can always settle up.
+- All balance entries (fines, manual charges, later no-show fees) count toward
+  every bar alike.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Holds must check `HOLD_BLOCK_AT` (5.00), not the borrowing bar.
+- `AccountBlocked` carries the member, balance and the bar that was hit, so the
+  desk can say why.
