+# 0004: No-show fee for uncollected holds (for later)
+
+## Context
+
+Holds are planned. A copy set aside for a member's hold is unavailable to everyone
+else; if the member never collects it, the library wants a small penalty. The owner
+stated this rule ahead of holds being built.
+
+## Decision
+
+- When a copy is set aside for a member's hold and they don't collect it within the
+  pickup time, they are charged a **no-show fee** of 1.00.
+- The fee is an account entry on the same balance as fines (ADR 0001), with its own
+  kind (`no_show`).
+- It counts toward the borrowing and hold bars like any fine (ADR 0003).
+- **Children never pay it**, just as they are never fined (ADR 0002).
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The holds feature needs a pickup-time policy value and a point where expiry is
+  detected; the fee is charged there.
+- The amount belongs in `lending.policy` alongside the fine rates.
