+# SPEC: Holds
+
+## Why
+
+When every copy of a title is out, members can only keep asking at the desk. With holds a member
+joins a queue for the title. When a copy comes back, it is set aside for whoever is first in line,
+and they get a few days to pick it up. A daily job clears holds nobody collected, and those members
+are charged a no-show fee (ADR 0004).
+
+Earlier spec: overdue fines and accounts, `docs/specs/overdue-fines.md`. Rules: `docs/adr/0003`
+(hold bar), `0004` (no-show fee), `0006` (holds). Amounts are in euros (€); the code only sees `Decimal`.
+
+## Interface (fixed by the owner; other code calls exactly this)
+
+- On `LendingService` in `src/lending/service.py`: `place_hold(member_id: str, isbn: str) -> Hold`,
+  `cancel_hold(hold_id: str) -> Hold`, `expire_holds() -> list[Hold]` (the daily job; returns the holds it
+  expired), `holds_for(isbn: str) -> list[Hold]` (active holds on the title, first in line first).
+  `return_copy` and `checkout` keep their signatures.
+- In `src/lending/models.py`: dataclass `Hold(hold_id: str, member_id: str, isbn: str, placed_on: date, status: HoldStatus, copy_id: str | None, pickup_by: date | None)`;
+  enum `HoldStatus` with `WAITING, READY, FULFILLED, CANCELLED, EXPIRED`; new member `CopyStatus.ON_HOLD_SHELF`.
+- Add `HoldNotAllowed(LendingError)` and `HoldNotFound(LendingError)` to `src/lending/errors.py`; keep using the existing error classes where they already fit.
+
+Added by this spec (follows ADR 0001): `EntryKind.NO_SHOW` for the no-show fee entry.
+
+## Terms
+
+- **Active hold**: a hold that is `WAITING` or `READY`.
+- **Waiting hold**: in the queue, no copy yet. **Ready hold**: a copy is on the hold shelf for it.
+- **Circulating copy**: any copy that is not `WITHDRAWN`.
+- **Set aside**: the copy becomes `ON_HOLD_SHELF`, the hold becomes `READY` with that `copy_id`,
+  and `pickup_by` is set.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+### Placing a hold
+- HP1. `place_hold` returns a `WAITING` hold for that member and title, with `placed_on` = today,
+  `copy_id` and `pickup_by` both `None`, and a hold id that no other hold has.
+- HP2. An unknown member raises `MemberNotFound`; an unknown ISBN raises `TitleNotFound`.
+- HP3. A member with a balance of €5.00 or more gets `AccountBlocked` (exactly €5.00 is blocked);
+  at €4.99 they can place the hold. The error carries the bar of 5.00, not the borrowing bar.
+- HP4. If any copy of the title is `AVAILABLE`, `place_hold` raises `HoldNotAllowed`. Copies on the hold shelf
+  for someone else count as out.
+- HP5. A member who already has an active hold on the title gets `HoldNotAllowed`.
+- HP6. A member who already has a copy of the title on loan gets `HoldNotAllowed`.
+- HP7. A title with no circulating copies (none at all, or all withdrawn) raises `HoldNotAllowed`.
+- HP8. Children can place holds under the same rules as adults.
+- HP9. There is no cap on how many active holds a member may have.
+- HP10. A refused `place_hold` creates no hold.
+
+### Queue and setting aside
+- HQ1. `holds_for(isbn)` returns the title's active holds in the order they were placed. It
+  leaves out fulfilled, cancelled and expired holds. An unknown ISBN raises `TitleNotFound`.
+- HQ2. When a copy is returned and the title has a waiting hold, the copy is set aside for the first
+  waiting hold in line, not put on the shelf. `return_copy` still returns the closed `Loan`, and any
+  overdue fine is charged as before.
+- HQ3. When a copy is returned and nobody is waiting, it goes back to `AVAILABLE` as before.
+- HQ4. `pickup_by` is 7 calendar days after the day the copy is set aside. If that is a Sunday, it
+  moves to the Monday.
+- HQ5. A copy added with `add_copy` to a title with a waiting hold is set aside for the first in line.
+- HQ6. A copy on the hold shelf is not in `available_copies` and cannot be withdrawn (`CopyNotAvailable`).
+
+### Collecting
+- HC1. The member a copy is set aside for can check it out up to and including `pickup_by`. The hold
+  becomes `FULFILLED` and drops out of `holds_for`.
+- HC2. Anyone else who tries to check out that copy gets `CopyNotAvailable`, and the hold stays `READY`.
+- HC3. Checkout rules still apply to the hold's member (borrowing bar, loan limit). A refused checkout
+  leaves the hold `READY` and the copy on the hold shelf.
+- HC4. A member who checks out a different copy of the same title while their hold is ready has that
+  hold `FULFILLED`. The copy that was set aside for them goes to the next waiting hold, or back to
+  `AVAILABLE` if nobody is waiting.
+
+### Cancelling
+- HX1. `cancel_hold` on a waiting hold makes it `CANCELLED` and returns it. The rest of the queue keeps its order.
+- HX2. `cancel_hold` on a ready hold makes it `CANCELLED` with no fee. Its copy goes straight to the
+  next waiting hold (new `pickup_by` counted from today), or back to `AVAILABLE`.
+- HX3. `cancel_hold` on a fulfilled, cancelled or expired hold raises `HoldNotAllowed` and changes nothing.
+- HX4. An unknown hold id raises `HoldNotFound`.
+
+### Expiry (the daily job)
+- HE1. `expire_holds()` makes every ready hold whose `pickup_by` is before today `EXPIRED`, and returns
+  exactly those holds, first in line first. A hold is not expired on its `pickup_by` day.
+- HE2. Each expired hold's copy goes to the next waiting hold, with `pickup_by` counted from the day the
+  job runs, or back to `AVAILABLE` if nobody is waiting.
+- HE3. An adult whose hold expires is charged a €1.00 no-show fee: one `no_show` account entry per expired
+  hold. It counts toward the borrowing and hold bars.
+- HE4. A child whose hold expires is not charged.
+- HE5. Waiting holds never expire, however long they have waited.
+- HE6. Running the job again on the same day expires nothing more and charges nothing more.
+
+### Unchanged
+- HU1. All existing behaviour and tests keep passing; titles without holds lend and return exactly as before.
+
+## Non-goals
+
+- Notifying members (email, SMS) that a copy is ready.
+- Changing the queue order: priority holds, or moving someone up the line.
+- Holds on one specific copy, or at a particular branch.
+- A cap on holds per member, or holds expiring while still waiting.
+- Re-queuing holds when the last circulating copy is withdrawn while people are waiting.
+- Renewals. These are next; ADR 0007 records the rules they must follow.
+- Persistence beyond the in-memory repository.
