index 0000000..e581170
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/specs/overdue-fines.md
@@ -0,0 +1,81 @@
+# SPEC: Overdue fines and member accounts
+
+## Why
+
+Late returns cost nothing today, so DVDs come back weeks late. Members now have an
+account: a late return charges an overdue fine, staff can add manual charges,
+members pay, and a member who owes too much cannot borrow.
+
+Amounts below are in euros (€); the code only sees `Decimal`.
+
+## Interface (fixed by the owner; other code calls exactly this)
+
+All on `LendingService` in `src/lending/service.py`:
+
+- `return_copy(copy_id)` keeps its signature and return value; a late return now also charges the fine.
+- `balance(member_id: str) -> Decimal` — what the member owes right now.
+- `add_charge(member_id: str, amount: Decimal, reason: str) -> Decimal` — manual staff charge; returns the new balance.
+- `pay(member_id: str, amount: Decimal) -> Decimal` — records a payment; returns the new balance.
+- Add to `src/lending/errors.py`: `AccountBlocked(LendingError)`, raised by `checkout` when the member
+  owes too much, and `InvalidAmount(LendingError)` for amounts that can't be accepted. Unknown members
+  keep raising `MemberNotFound`.
+
+Added by this spec (owner left the choice open): `InvalidReason(LendingError)` in
+`src/lending/errors.py`, raised by `add_charge` for a blank reason.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+### Late days
+- A1. A copy returned on or before its due date has 0 late days and charges nothing.
+- A2. Late days are the days after the due date up to and including the return day,
+  not counting days the library is closed (Sundays).
+- A3. Book due Mon 23 March 2026, returned Mon 30 March 2026 → 6 late days (Sun 29 excluded).
+
+### Fine amount
+- F1. An adult's fine is late days × rate: books €0.25 per late day, DVDs €1.00 per late day.
+- F2. Example A3 charges €1.50.
+- F3. The fine for one loan never exceeds the title's replacement cost; above that it equals the replacement cost.
+- F4. Children are never fined: a child's late return closes the loan and shelves the copy as usual,
+  and their balance does not change.
+- F5. Fines are charged only when the copy comes back: an overdue copy still out adds nothing to the balance.
+- F6. Each late return adds its own fine; two late returns add two fines.
+- F7. `return_copy` returns the same `Loan` it did before (closed, `returned_on` set), late or not.
+
+### Balance
+- B1. A newly registered member's balance is `Decimal("0.00")`.
+- B2. Balance = sum of all fines and charges − sum of all payments.
+- B3. `balance`, `add_charge` and `pay` raise `MemberNotFound` for an unknown member.
+- B4. The balance is never negative.
+
+### Manual charges
+- C1. `add_charge` adds `amount` to the balance and returns the new balance.
+- C2. Manual charges apply to any member, children included (the child exemption covers fines only).
+- C3. `add_charge` with a blank or whitespace-only reason raises `InvalidReason`, and the balance does not change.
+
+### Payments
+- P1. `pay` subtracts `amount` from the balance and returns the new balance; partial payments are allowed.
+- P2. Paying exactly the balance brings it to 0.00.
+- P3. Paying more than the balance raises `InvalidAmount`, and the balance does not change.
+
+### Amounts
+- M1. A charge or payment must be positive and in whole cents. Zero, negative amounts, or amounts with
+  sub-cent precision (e.g. `Decimal("0.005")`) raise `InvalidAmount`, and the balance does not change.
+- M2. Floats, NaN/infinity and non-numbers raise `InvalidAmount`; `int` amounts are accepted as whole euros.
+
+### Blocking
+- K1. `checkout` raises `AccountBlocked` when the member's balance is €10.00 or more (exactly €10.00 is blocked).
+- K2. With a balance of €9.99 the member can borrow.
+- K3. A blocked checkout creates no loan and leaves the copy available.
+- K4. Paying the balance below €10.00 lifts the block.
+- K5. Only `checkout` is blocked: a blocked member can still return copies, pay and receive charges.
+- K6. `checkout` for an unknown member still raises `MemberNotFound`.
+
+## Non-goals
+
+- Waiving or refunding a charge.
+- Viewing a member's list of charges and payments. Entries are still recorded individually
+  (date, kind, amount, reason, loan) so this can be added later.
+- Account credit or overpayment.
+- Fines that build up on copies still out (no accrual before return).
+- Holds, no-show fees and renewals. These are planned; see `docs/adr/` for the rules they must follow.
+- Persistence beyond the in-memory repository.
